  "Description": {
    "Cost": 9607933,
    "UIName": "Grasshopper",
    "Id": "chassisdef_grasshopper_GHR-QS1",
    "Name": "Grasshopper",
    "Details": "Quicsell's Heavy Laser Sniper. The GHR-QS1 boasts a huge array of lethal laser firepower. LBX Large Lasers for shooting down pesky lights and VTOLs, and Large REX Lasers (King of the battlefield) for any mech that dares to get too close. All kept nice and cool by our one-of-a-kind outsourced fuelcell engine using the finest  Periphery technologies.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Rugged</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.08</color></b>",
    "Icon": "uixTxrIcon_grasshopper"
  },
  "VariantName": "GHR-QS1",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "QuicsellOmni",
      "skip_hardpoint",
      "unit_mechtool"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Heavy Laser Sniper",
  "YangsThoughts": "On the one hand, that fuel cell is a work of art. Totally irreplaceable, and unreproducable. I don't know what 'contractors' (read: pirates) they got to make the thing, but they certainly managed to do something amazing. On the OTHER hand (the metal one, in case you were wondering), it's an abomination against all traditional mech engineering, and I'll be amazed if you don't blow yourself up with it at some point. So it's a bit of a tossup, really.",
